  "result": "Perfect! All 230 tests pass (including 20 new vatSummary tests). Here's what I've implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\n**`src/reports.js`** now includes:\n\n1. **`overdueInvoices(invoices, asOf)`** \u2014 Already created in previous task\n   - Filters invoices with status 'issued' or 'partially_paid'\n   - Returns overdue invoices sorted by most overdue first\n   - Returns: `{ number, customerId, dueDate, daysOverdue, due }`\n\n2. **`vatSummary(invoices)`** \u2014 Newly added function\n   - Filters invoices with status 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid' (excludes draft and paid invoices in terms of payment status)\n   - Aggregates by VAT rate\n   - Calculates `base` = line total after discounts (qty \u00d7 unitPrice \u2212 discount)\n   - Calculates `vat` = base \u00d7 (rate / 100), rounded\n   - Returns: `[{ rate, base, vat }]` sorted by rate descending (highest to lowest)\n   - Properly handles discounts and multiple lines per VAT rate\n\n**`test/reports.test.js`** \u2014 20 comprehensive vatSummary tests covering:\n- Empty arrays and no applicable invoices\n- Single and multiple invoices\n- Different invoice statuses (issued, partially_paid, paid)\n- Multiple VAT rates (0%, 9%, 21%)\n- Sorting by rate descending\n- Aggregation of multiple lines\n- Various discount scenarios (0%, 5%, 10%, 100%)\n- Fractional VAT calculations with proper rounding\n- High-value invoices\n- Edge cases and immutability\n\nAll 230 tests pass successfully.",
